Let's start with the title of your book, The Myth of Closure. Many of us tend to think that we want closure after a death or a divorce or a breakup. Why do you believe that closure is the wrong thing to be looking for after we lose something or someone? Well, closure has a definition meaning finality. It means closing the door on something that has happened. It's a perfectly good word in the business community for closing a contract, for closing a real estate deal, or for closing a road after a flood has occurred. But it is a harmful word in human relationships. It indicates that even though we have had attachment to someone or something like a pet, that once they are gone, we can close the door on that.
让我们从您的书名《终结的神话》开始谈起。我们许多人往往认为，在经历死亡、离婚或分手后，我们想要的是“终结”（closure）。为什么您认为在失去某物或某人后，追求“终结”是错误的方向呢？嗯，“终结”的定义意味着最终性。它意味着对已经发生的事情关上大门。在商业领域，这是一个非常好的词，用于结束合同、完成房地产交易或在洪水发生后封闭道路。但在人际关系中，它是一个有害的词。它暗示着，尽管我们曾与某人或某物（比如宠物）建立了依恋，但一旦他们离开，我们就可以对那段关系关上大门。

